# Weight profile hy4-3.56: Tencent's Hy4-flash in our EXL3 pack at 3.56 bpw (experts at 3.5 bits, attention, shared
# experts, the head and the Engram tables at 5), converted from the BF16 checkpoint at revision d88c9dfd with a
# templated chat calibration. 112.38 GB on disk with its tables. The recommended pack. Switch with
# ops/use-profile.sh hy4-3.56.
QSE_HY4_BPW=3.56
QSE_WEIGHTS_HF=0xBakeer/TandemLLM-Hy4-flash-EXL3-3.5
QSE_WEIGHTS_REVISION=main
QSE_WEIGHTS_GB=112.38
# MemAvailable (GiB) a start needs: the load took 78.1 GiB at 262,144 tokens, plus the server's prefill workspace
# estimate at that window (7.3) and the 15 GiB floor
QSE_MEM_NEED_GIB=101
# OPS-308: the engine's limits, as every family's; ENG-609: derived as Flash-Next's (flashnext-3.05.env), from what
# was measured under the allocator's expandable segments (_hy4.env). Ceiling: the 8-lane load on hy4-3.56 reserves
# 71.84 GiB (2026-11-24), + 0.90 for the figure's one-lane basis (with the pool the policy takes slot 0's window off,
# 4.12, and adds the side slots' share, 3.22) + 6 for the caches (Flash-Next's figure; 1.3 to 3.4 GiB held while
# served) = 78.74 -> 79, enforced 78.10 at 8 lanes; peak: 78.74 + the prefill workspace where it stops growing
# (engine/models/hy4_flash/serving.py WS_CAP, 2.25 GiB; 1.81 measured at 249,971 tokens) = 80.99 -> 81, enforced 80.10.
# Both packs take the same. Before: 85 / 92, the one-lane reserve of hold 1b + 12 and the 27B's workspace line at
# 262,144 tokens (7.3), neither measured on Hy4-flash, and the box had 18.3 GiB left at that peak: the residency
# planner refused every decision model (floor + margin 19)
MEM_CEILING_GIB=79
MEM_PEAK_GIB=81
. "${REPO}/ops/profiles/_hy4.env"
